   "final_message": "All 6 sweep points are clean with `width=9` (4.14 \u00b5m). Width=8 fails at L=0.25 with an N-well/P-Diffusion spacing violation, so width=9 is the narrowest achievable.\n\n**Final status:** CLEAN at all 6 sweep points. Compacted from width=10 (4.6 \u00b5m) to width=9 (4.14 \u00b5m).\n\n**What was hard:** The compaction was constrained by the N-well/P-diffusion spacing rule (diff/tap.8, 0.18 \u00b5m). At L=0.25, the required span grows enough that width=8 (3.68 \u00b5m) causes the n-well to encroach on the p-diffusion. Width=9 (4.14 \u00b5m) provides just enough room to stay clean across the entire sweep, including the widest L=0.25 case. The existing parametric layout already derived all dimensions from L and the parameters, so no geometry changes were needed \u2014 only reducing the column count from 10 to 9.",
